<figure id="A8.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Performance on the <span id="A8.T13.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">False Presuppositions</span> and <span id="A8.T13.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scientific References</span> tasks from <span id="A8.T13.8" class="ltx_text">HALoGEN</span> when synthesizing responses from small model sizes. We report Response Ratio (R<math id="A8.T13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>) and Hallucination Score (H<math id="A8.T13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>), both lower is better. Consensus decoding with <span id="A8.T13.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ConGrs</span> consistently achieves low Response Ratio and Hallucination Score.</figcaption>
